DirectGate Agent\par
\par
Operational disclosure\par
\par
This installer registers one auto-start Windows service named directgate-agent. The service runs only a small privilege-separation launcher as LocalSystem. The launcher reads the machine-wide config, obtains the configured shell.user's logged-on user token, and starts the actual DirectGate agent in that user's session. Terminal sessions, file-manager operations, protocol parsing, and network session handling run as shell.user, not as LocalSystem.\par
\par
Remote access is not available until the device is explicitly paired with a DirectGate account and authenticated. DirectGate uses SRP authentication and encrypted post-authentication sessions; the installed service does not grant anonymous remote access.\par
